{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7e4c1a2-9f3d-4a6b-8c21-workshopapi001",
    "name": "API Workshop - Procurement Invoices",
    "description": "Hands-on API workshop: connection, data structure, pagination,\nflattening, and error handling.\n\nGETTING STARTED\n1. Pick the 'Workshop API (local)' environment, top right.\n2. Open folder 1 and run C1.\n3. That is it -- the bearer token is fetched automatically and\n   refreshed when it expires. You never paste a token by hand.\n\nRequests whose names say '-> 422' or '-> 503' are SUPPOSED to fail.\nTheir descriptions explain what to look for.\n\nEvery request has a description. Read them: they are the workbook.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Fetches a bearer token automatically, so every request just works after",
          "// import. Skips itself for the token endpoint, and reuses a token that is",
          "// still valid for at least another minute.",
          "const path = String(pm.request.url.getPath() || '');",
          "const isTokenCall = path.indexOf('/auth/token') !== -1;",
          "const token = pm.environment.get('token');",
          "const expiresAt = pm.environment.get('token_expires_at');",
          "",
          "let stillValid = false;",
          "if (token && expiresAt) {",
          "    stillValid = (new Date(expiresAt).getTime() - Date.now()) > 60000;",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (!isTokenCall && !stillValid) {",
          "    const base = pm.environment.get('base_url');",
          "    pm.sendRequest({",
          "        url: base + '/v1/auth/token',",
          "        method: 'POST',",
          "        header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },",
          "        body: {",
          "            mode: 'urlencoded',",
          "            urlencoded: [",
          "                { key: 'username', value: pm.environment.get('username') },",
          "                { key: 'password', value: pm.environment.get('password') }",
          "            ]",
          "        }",
          "    }, function (err, res) {",
          "        if (err) {",
          "            console.error('Auto-login failed:', err);",
          "            return;",
          "        }",
          "        if (res.code !== 200) {",
          "            console.error('Auto-login got HTTP ' + res.code + ': ' + res.text());",
          "            return;",
          "        }",
          "        const body = res.json();",
          "        pm.environment.set('token', body.access_token);",
          "        pm.environment.set('token_expires_at', body.expires_at);",
          "        console.log('Token refreshed, expires ' + body.expires_at);",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Connection (C1-C3)",
      "description": "Reach the API, get a token, then prove the token works. Do these in order.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "C1  GET /v1/ping  (no auth)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/ping",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "ping"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Is the API reachable at all? No token needed.\n\nIf this fails, it is a network problem, not an auth problem:\n  - wrong host or port\n  - http:// vs https://\n  - a proxy or VPN in the way\n  - on Azure, a 20-30s cold start on the very first call\n\nCheck app_version / git_commit / uptime_seconds in the body to\nconfirm which deployment you're actually talking to. A restart\nresets uptime_seconds and re-runs the seed, so data and logins\ncome back exactly as before -- but expect a few extra seconds\non the very next request while that happens.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('reports ok', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('ok');",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "console.log('app_version=' + body.app_version +",
                  "    ' git_commit=' + body.git_commit +",
                  "    ' uptime_seconds=' + body.uptime_seconds);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "C2a  POST /v1/auth/token  with JSON  -> 422 (expected failure)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "This SHOULD fail with 422. It is here on purpose.\n\nThe endpoint expects form-encoded fields, not JSON. Read the\nerror body: it tells you username and password are missing --\nbecause the server never looked in the JSON body for them.\n\nNow compare with C2b.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"{{username}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 422', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('complains the fields are missing', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('username');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "C2b  POST /v1/auth/token  form-encoded  -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The same credentials, sent as x-www-form-urlencoded. This works.\n\nThe token is saved to the environment automatically, so every\nother request in this collection can use it.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "urlencoded",
              "urlencoded": [
                {
                  "key": "username",
                  "value": "{{username}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "password",
                  "value": "{{password}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('returns a bearer token', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('access_token');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('token', body.access_token);",
                  "pm.environment.set('token_expires_at', body.expires_at);",
                  "console.log('Token saved. Expires ' + body.expires_at);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "C3a  GET /v1/whoami  no header  -> 403",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/whoami",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "whoami"
              ]
            },
            "description": "No Authorization header at all -> 403 Forbidden.\n\nCompare with C3b, which sends a *bad* token and gets 401.\nTwo different codes for two different situations:\n  403 = you did not present credentials\n  401 = you presented credentials and they were rejected\n\nMany people expect these the other way around. Worth a think.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 403', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(403);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "C3b  GET /v1/whoami  bad token  -> 401",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer this-is-not-a-real-token"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/whoami",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "whoami"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A syntactically fine but invalid token -> 401 Unauthorized.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 401', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "C3c  GET /v1/whoami  valid token  -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/whoami",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "whoami"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Who am I, and when does my token expire?\n\ntoken_expires_in_seconds is the useful one: if requests suddenly\nstart returning 401 mid-session, check here first."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('token has time left', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.token_expires_in_seconds).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "console.log('Logged in as ' + body.username +",
                  "    ', token valid for ' + Math.round(body.token_expires_in_seconds / 60) + ' min');",
                  "console.log('Rate limit remaining: ' +",
                  "    pm.response.headers.get('x-ratelimit-remaining'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Data structure (D1-D3)",
      "description": "Work out the shape of the data before you write any code against it.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "D1  GET /openapi.json  (the machine-readable contract)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/openapi.json",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "openapi.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The full API contract as JSON. Every field, every type.\n\nFind the InvoiceOut schema and list its fields with their types.\nThe human-friendly version of this is at {{base_url}}/docs",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "D2  GET /v1/invoices/{number}  one fully nested invoice",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/invoices/{{sample_invoice}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "invoices",
                "{{sample_invoice}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "One invoice, fully expanded. This is the shape you will flatten.\n\nMap the nesting and mark the cardinality of each level:\n  invoice -> line_items[] -> postings[]\n\nNote vendor_number is a plain field on the invoice, NOT a nested\nobject -- resolving it to a name/address means calling\nGET /v1/master-data/vendors separately. That is deliberate: it is\nhow a real transactional extract references master data.\n\nHow many rows would a fully exploded flat table have for THIS\none invoice? (lines x postings per line)"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const inv = pm.response.json();",
                  "const lines = inv.line_items || [];",
                  "const postings = lines.reduce((n, li) => n + (li.postings || []).length, 0);",
                  "console.log(inv.invoice_number + ' (vendor ' + inv.vendor_number + '): ' +",
                  "    lines.length + ' lines, ' + postings +",
                  "    ' postings -> ' + postings + ' rows when fully exploded');",
                  "const firstAmount = lines[0].postings[0].line_amount;",
                  "pm.test('line_amount is a STRING, not a number', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(firstAmount).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "D3  POST /v1/invoices/search  page_size=1",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/invoices/search",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "invoices",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The same nesting, but wrapped in a paginated envelope.\n\nNote the three top-level keys: data, page, meta.\nThe rows are in `data` -- not at the top level.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"page_size\": 1\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Pagination (P1-P2)",
      "description": "Two different pagination styles, one per endpoint -- because you will meet both in the wild.\n\nMaster data uses limit/offset. Invoice search uses cursors.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "P1a  master-data  limit=5  offset=0",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/master-data/vendors?limit=5&offset=0",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "master-data",
                "vendors"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Offset pagination. Look at the `page` object:\n  total       how many there are altogether\n  has_more    is there another page\n  next_offset the offset to ask for next (null on the last page)\n\nBefore running P1b: what will has_more be? Predict, then check."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const p = pm.response.json().page;",
                  "console.log('total=' + p.total + ' returned=' + p.returned +",
                  "    ' has_more=' + p.has_more + ' next_offset=' + p.next_offset);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P1b  master-data  limit=5  offset=5",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/master-data/vendors?limit=5&offset=5",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "master-data",
                "vendors"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "5"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Page 2. Same total, different rows."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P1c  master-data  offset past the end  -> 200 with []",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/master-data/vendors?limit=5&offset=99999",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "master-data",
                "vendors"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "5"
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "99999"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Asking beyond the last row is NOT an error. You get 200 with an\nempty items array and has_more=false.\n\n'No results' and 'something went wrong' are different things, and\nyour extraction code has to tell them apart."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200, not 404', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('items is empty', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().items).to.be.an('array').that.is.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P1d  master-data  limit=999  -> 422",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/master-data/vendors?limit=999",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "master-data",
                "vendors"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "999"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "There is a hard cap on page size. Asking for more is rejected.\n\nRead the cap out of the error body rather than the docs -- that is\nwhat you would have to do against a real vendor API."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 422', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(422);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P2a  search  page 1  (saves next_cursor)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/invoices/search",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "invoices",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Cursor pagination. Note what `page` does and does not contain:\n  next_cursor      an opaque token for the next page\n  estimated_total  present on page 1 ONLY\n\nThere is no page count. Run P2b to see why that matters.\n\nThe cursor is saved to {{next_cursor}} for you.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"page_size\": 10\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const p = pm.response.json().page;",
                  "pm.environment.set('next_cursor', p.next_cursor);",
                  "console.log('estimated_total=' + p.estimated_total);",
                  "console.log('next_cursor=' + p.next_cursor);",
                  "console.log('(decode it: it is just base64 JSON)');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P2b  search  page 2  via next_cursor",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/invoices/search",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "invoices",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Page 2, using the cursor P2a saved.\n\nLook at estimated_total now. It is null.\n\nSo you cannot compute 'total / page_size' to know when to stop.\nThe only correct rule is: keep going until next_cursor is null.\nThat is deliberate -- it is how most real cursor APIs behave.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"page_size\": 10,\n  \"cursor\": \"{{next_cursor}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 200', function () {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "});",
                  "const p = pm.response.json().page;",
                  "pm.test('estimated_total is null on page 2', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(p.estimated_total).to.be.null;",
                  "});",
                  "pm.environment.set('next_cursor', p.next_cursor);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "P2c  search  broken cursor  -> 400",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/invoices/search",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "invoices",
                "search"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A malformed cursor gives 400, not 422.\n\nThe difference: 422 means the request was the wrong SHAPE.\n400 here means the shape was fine but the VALUE was meaningless.\nWorth distinguishing when you are writing error handling.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"page_size\": 10,\n  \"cursor\": \"not-a-real-cursor\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('status is 400', function () {",
